===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|merke}}, {{m|enm|mirke}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mirce|t=dark, gloomy, evil}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*merkuz|t=dark}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mergʷ-|t=to flicker; to darken; to be dark}}. Cognate {{cog|da|mørk|t=dark}}, {{cog|no|mørk|t=dark}}, {{cog|sv|mörk|t=dark}}, {{cog|is|myrkur|t=dark}}, as also {{cog|sq|murg|t=dark}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*morkъ|t=darkness}}, {{cog|lt|márgas|t=multicolored}}, {{cog|grc|ἀμορβός|t=dark}}.

